---
import Doc from '../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import FoundationPager from '../../components/FoundationPager.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';

const title = 'Harness reference';
const description =
  'Which harnesses read AGENTS.md, and the short list of cases where one still needs a file of its own.';
---

<Doc title={title} description={description} section="foundation">
  <p class="doc-lede">
    Where each harness expects context files. The source of truth
    <a href={url('commands/init/')}><code>init</code></a>,
    <a href={url('commands/document/')}><code>document</code></a>, and
    <a href={url('commands/scope/')}><code>scope</code></a> read from.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Last verified: 2026-11-21</strong> against each vendor's own docs.
    Where a number or field name is not documented, this page says so rather
    than inventing one. A stale source of truth is confidently wrong, which is
    the failure this skill exists to stop.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    <code>AGENTS.md</code> at the repo root is read by every harness below. It
    is plain Markdown with no schema, stewarded by the Linux Foundation's
    Agentic AI Foundation. Emit it first; emit anything else only when a
    harness needs something <code>AGENTS.md</code> cannot express.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Harness</th><th>Reads <code>AGENTS.md</code>?</th><th>Its own file</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Claude Code</td>
        <td>Yes, v2.1.277+, when no <code>CLAUDE.md</code> sits above the working directory</td>
        <td><code>CLAUDE.md</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Cursor</td>
        <td>Yes, root and subdirectories</td>
        <td><code>.cursor/rules/*.mdc</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Codex / generic</td>
        <td>Yes — this is its native file</td>
        <td>—</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>GitHub Copilot</td>
        <td>Cloud agent, code review, CLI, VS Code Chat. <strong>Not</strong> GitHub.com Chat</td>
        <td><code>.github/copilot-instructions.md</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Windsurf</td>
        <td>Yes, root and intermediate directories</td>
        <td><code>.windsurf/rules/*.md</code></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Per-harness locations, frontmatter schemas, skill-portability limits,
    plugins and validation commands live in the skill's
    <code>reference/harness-detail.md</code>, loaded on demand rather than at
    session start.
  </p>

  <h2>Which to target</h2>
  <p>
    Ask the user. Then emit <code>AGENTS.md</code> and stop, unless one of
    these applies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Rules must be scoped to file patterns.</strong>
      <code>AGENTS.md</code> has no globs. Add <code>.cursor/rules/*.mdc</code>,
      <code>.github/instructions/*.instructions.md</code>, or
      <code>.claude/rules/*.md</code> with <code>paths:</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A <code>CLAUDE.md</code> already exists.</strong> Claude Code
      reads it and skips <code>AGENTS.md</code>. Reduce it to a single
      <code>@AGENTS.md</code> import rather than maintaining two files.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>GitHub.com Chat matters.</strong> It reads
      <code>.github/copilot-instructions.md</code> but not
      <code>AGENTS.md</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The repo is multi-package.</strong> Nest an
      <code>AGENTS.md</code> per package; every harness above reads the nearest.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Do not emit a pointer file per harness by reflex. That pattern predates
    native <code>AGENTS.md</code> support and now costs maintenance for nothing.
  </p>

  <h2><code>docs/agents/</code>: harness-agnostic overflow</h2>
  <p>
    When <code>AGENTS.md</code> grows past ~80 lines, per-area conventions
    split into <code>docs/agents/&lt;area&gt;.md</code>. No harness auto-loads
    this, but any agent can be told to read it. Reference from
    <code>AGENTS.md</code>'s "See also".
  </p>

  <h2><code>.claude/rules/</code>: the Claude Code auto-load layer</h2>
  <p>
    Claude Code reads every file in this directory at launch, <strong>unless</strong>
    the file carries <code>paths:</code> frontmatter, which scopes it to
    matching files. No other harness reads <code>.claude/</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>paths:</code> is the mechanism to reach for — it does the same job as
    Cursor's <code>globs</code> and Copilot's <code>applyTo</code>. Numeric
    filename prefixes still set load order for unscoped files, but ordering
    matters far less than scoping.
  </p>

  <FoundationPager slug="harness-reference" />
</Doc>
